  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive material decays by simultaneous emissions of two particles with half lives of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1400</mn></math> years and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn></math> years, respectively. What will be the time after the which one third of the material remains ? (Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)",
    "image": null
